1
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
A comedy that proves love is blind.

2
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Love and Other Disasters is a comedy, romance film directed by Alek Keshishian.

3
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Flighty Emily "Jacks" Jackson works for the British edition of Vogue magazine.

4
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Rather than pursue a relationship, Jacks regularly hooks up with her devoted
ex-boyfriend, James Wildstone, and lives with Peter Simon, a gay screenwriter.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
When Jacks meets Argentinian photographer's assistant Paolo Sarmiento, she assumes he is gay and tries
to bring him and Peter together, unaware that Paolo is straight and in love with her.

6
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Emily Jackson, played by Brittany Murphy.

7
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Peter Simon, played by Matthew Rhys.

8
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Paolo Sarmiento, played by Santiago Cabrera.

9
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Tallulah Wentworth, played by Catherine Tate.

10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Finlay, played by Jamie Sives.

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Felicity Wentworth, played by Stephanie Beacham.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Love and Other Disasters is a 2006 romantic comedy film
written and directed by Alek Keshishian.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
It had its world premiere at the 2006 Toronto International Film Festival.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
In 2008, the film had its UK premiere in London as the gala screening
for the BFI 22nd London Gay and Lesbian Film Festival.

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Brittany Murphy portrays an assistant at British Vogue who is the
catalyst for a group of young friends as they try to find love.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
Outfest 2007 presented the film as one of their features.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Keshishian originally wanted Gwyneth Paltrow to play
Jacks, but she was pregnant at the time.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Paltrow was later given a cameo role.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film explores themes of new love, london,
england, vernissage, screenplay, lifestyle.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
